* RFO match:\n \nQ = (50/15.5 - 1)^0.5 = 1.492\nRs = 15.5\nXs = 2 * 22/7 * L * f + 10.8\nRp = 50\n \nDC Block X @ 915 MHz = 1.22 Ohms\n \n(X_L + 10.8 - 1.22)/ 15.5 = 1.492\nX_L = (1.492 * 15.5 - 10.8 + 1.22)\nX_L = 13.54 Ohms\n \n50 / X_C = 1.492\nX_C = 33.512 Ohms\n \nChoosen: X_C = 33.59 Ohms and \n         X_L = 13.3 Ohms\n \nCould use some tuning, not 100% necessary
* Bias Tee Sizing: (All values taken from SimSurf/KSIM/Samsung MLCC)\n \nTargeting Z @ 915 Mhz of L > 1500 Ohms and of C to be < 5 Ohms\n \nSRF of 0603 220nH wire wound inductor = 1330 MHz\n \nAnd Z @ 915MHz = 2290 Ohms\n \nZ @ 915 MHz of 33pF COG 0603 = 2.68 Ohms\nSRF = 1.3GHz\n \nChoosen Values: 220nH and 33pF
.include Spice_Models/GCM1885C1H4R7CA16_0603_C0G_4.7pF_50V.mod
* 2nd Harmonic Notch Filter:\n \nNotch Frequency = 1.83GHz\n \n1.83 * 10^(9) = 1 / (2 * 22/7 * (L * C)^0.5)\n \nL * C = 7.557 * 10^(-21)\n \nX_L / X_C = 1\n \nImpedence: X_L * X_C = 2500\n \nX_L = X_C = 50R\n \nAfter tuning with real spice models, \nverified notch at 1.827GHz with \n-24.5dB attenuation.\n \nZout of 2nd Harmonic filter is 50.408 + 13.88i R
