* 1st Harmonic Low Pass Butterworth Filter:\n \nCorner Frequency = 1.8GHz\n \n1.8 * 10^(9) = 1 / (22/7 * (L * C)^0.5)\n \n|L * C| = 3.124 * 10^(−20)\n \nX_L / X_C = 4\n \nImpedence: X_L * X_C = 2500\n \n4 * X_C^2 = 2500\n \nX_C = 25R\n \nX_L = 100R\n \nNeeded to push corner freq above 915MHz to keep \n915MHz inside pass band and around 50R\n \nAfter tuning freq response and real part of impedence\nto be around 50R, went with 8.7nH and 2.9pF
